      {
        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "c69d6acf-a489-5c49-bad9-1d3746869615",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Films: The Strongest Man in the World, Candleshoe, Now You See Him, Now You Don't, The Computer Wore Tennis Shoes\n- People: Kurt Russell, Jodie Foster, David Niven, Helen Hayes, Leo McKern, Winifred Deforest Coffin, Michael Innes\n- Organizations: Disney, Walt Disney Productions\n- Places: Medfield College\n- Topics: film sequels, television appearances\n\nFacts:\n- \"Now You See Him, Now You Don't\" is a sequel to the 1969 film \"The Computer Wore Tennis Shoes.\"\n- \"Now You See Him, Now You Don't\" was followed by the 1975 film \"The Strongest Man in the World.\"\n- \"The Strongest Man in the World\" is a 1975 Disney film starring Kurt Russell as a student at the fictional Medfield College.\n- Winifred Deforest Coffin appeared in the Hollywood film \"Now You See Him, Now You Don't.\"\n- Winifred Deforest Coffin also appeared in television shows including \"Adam-12,\" \"The Doris Day Show,\" \"The Debbie Reynolds Show,\" \"Lancer,\" \"The Beverly Hillbillies,\" \"High Chaparral,\" \"Death Valley Days,\" \"Petticoat Junction,\" \"Perry Mason,\" \"Bonanza,\" \"Bewitched,\" \"Honey West,\" and \"The Ann Sothern Show.\"\n- \"Candleshoe\" is a 1977 American family adventure film produced by Walt Disney Productions.\n- \"Candleshoe\" is based on Michael Innes's novel \"Christmas at Candleshoe.\"\n- \"Candleshoe\" stars Jodie Foster, David Niven, Helen Hayes in her last big screen appearance, and Leo McKern.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
